<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Wizlock (250)</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>wizlock             (lock out all mortals; or, if locked, unlock)
wizlock &lt;level&gt;     (lock out that level and below)
wizlock 0           (only stop new characters)
</pre>
<p>Closes the game to players below a level, for maintenance or testing.
</p>
<ul><li><b>wizlock</b> alone locks out everyone below level 220, the mortals and the lesser immortals. If the game is already wizlocked, wizlock alone unlocks it.</li>
<li><b>wizlock &lt;level&gt;</b> locks out that level and every level below it. You can never lock out your own level or higher.</li>
<li><b>wizlock 0</b> only stops new characters from being made.</li></ul>
<p>While the game is wizlocked, no new characters can be made at all. A 
player who is locked out is told "Sorry, the game is wizlocked for your 
level." when they log in, and disconnected. Those already in the game 
stay. The lock is lifted when the game reboots. It is logged.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Ban</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Reboot</a>
</pre>




</div>